    "result": "Excellent! I have successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Complete\n\n### What was added:\n\n**CLI Changes** (`frai-cli/src/index.ts`):\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable)\n- Created `parseThresholds()` function to validate format and range (0-1)\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to:\n  - Validate threshold format and values\n  - Check for unknown metrics against available evaluations\n  - Pass thresholds to `generateReport()`\n  - Exit 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass, 2 for usage errors\n\n**Core Changes** (`frai-core/src/eval/`):\n- `index.js`: Updated `generateReport()` to accept `thresholds` parameter and add `passed` and `thresholds` fields to reports\n- `reporters.js`: Updated markdown reporter to include \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n- `index.test.js`: Added comprehensive tests covering all threshold scenarios\n\n**Documentation** (both READMEs):\n- Documented the new `--threshold` option with examples and metric IDs\n\n### Key Features:\n- \u2705 Multiple `--threshold` options supported\n- \u2705 Validation: `<metric>=<number>`, value must be 0-1\n- \u2705 Thresholds pass when score \u2265 minimum\n- \u2705 Metrics with no score fail their thresholds\n- \u2705 JSON: Added `passed` bool and `thresholds` list with `{metric, min, score, passed}`\n- \u2705 Markdown: New \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status\n- \u2705 Exit codes: 0 (all pass or no thresholds), 1 (any fail), 2 (usage error)\n- \u2705 Works with custom metrics\n- \u2705 Fully backward compatible\n- \u2705 SDK support via frai-core\n\nThe feature is ready and follows your specification exactly.",
